      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ok, I think I understand: Enabling CONFIG_EXPERIMENTAL_CONSOLE strips out all the interactive console functionality (echo and so on) from the EC code, and instead expects commands to arrive in a special format preceded with two ampersands.  Even though I am not using servod, I could change my host-side code (OpenTitan tool) to emit the commands in this ampersand format.  (I have not read the EC-3PO document fully, but I expect that output from the commands also arrives in an encoded format, allowing it to be distinguished from general debug logging.)\n\nWith that, my concern about partial commands sitting in the buffer and causing problems would be addressed, as I assume that EC would recognize two ampersands \"in the middle\" of a command to mean that the previous partial command needs to be discarded, and parsing of a new command should begin.\n\nIf my understanding is correct, I can abandon this CL.",
      "parentUuid": "963a7563_a6c5b147",
